ot, maybe we kill the renderer or DCHECK here."],["4f9f744f_57d23f54",4,-15,1,"Doesn't look like this is covered by tests. When could we ever hit this? Can we DCEHCK here instead, or kill the renderer otherwise?"]],0,294],[7253171,20433,46,1.326,1.047,[[3,0.704,42,32],[2,0.296,16,14]],[],0,295],[7243395,20437,155,3.934,3.229,[[13,0.557,71,87],[7,0.443,85,68]],[],0,296],[7263184,20437,16,0.721,0.543,[[14,0.85,22,14],[12,0.15,33,2]],[["556f9d8f_6664fe0d",44,0,1,"```suggestion \"Enables the Glic actor cursor\"; ```"],["86521f50_b24588db",45,0,1,"Please keep this sorted together with the other glic-actor flags above"],["bc815b3d_83c1f798",44,0,1,"```suggestion inline constexpr char kGlicActorCursorName[] = \"Glic actor cursor\"; ```"]],0,297],[7276425,20441,187,4.195,3.394,[[3,43]],[],0,298],[7276429,20441,68,2.344,1.853,[[3,44]],[],0,299],[7282920,20445,88,2.252,1.833,[[13,0.733,72,65],[7,0.267,86,23]],[["213c9950_11ac8d8a",11,-1,1,"nit: set these to currentX and currentY and then pass those values into setCursorTransform"],["2a8839f7_dc247e32",13,-1,1,"seems like this test and the one below share a lot of duplicated code, can you make a helped function and just pass in X,Y coords?"],["4fbeeb3c_e125df91",11,-1,1,"nit: reword before calculating the cursor movement to the target"]],0,300],[7302405,20445,212,4.195,3.394,[[3,45]],[],0,301],[7311465,20445,3,0.142,0.088,[[7,87]],[],0,302]]}